# Signature blobs must never be diffed as text.
#
# A raw Ed25519 signature is 64 bytes that usually contain no NUL, so git's
# "is this binary?" heuristic calls it TEXT and emits the raw bytes into every
# diff. The pre-push sensitivity guard pipes `git log -p` through awk, and awk
# dies on those bytes with "towc: multibyte conversion failure" — which means
# the file is SILENTLY UNSCANNED rather than loudly rejected. Marking the path
# `-diff` makes git print "Binary files differ" instead, so the guard's scanner
# always sees well-formed text.
#
# scripts/fixtures/ now commits signatures as base64 TEXT (*.producer.sig.b64),
# so this rule should never fire in normal use; it is the backstop that keeps a
# stray raw signature from quietly disabling the guard again.
*.producer.sig -diff
*.sig -diff
